", "lp": -0.0002611620584502816, "top": [["_COMPILER", -0.0002611620584502816], [" Compiler", -10.256353378295898]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.0005145204486325383, "top": [["=", -0.0005145204486325383], ["\n", -11.741238594055176]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -3.5167358873877674e-05, "top": [["ic", -3.5167358873877674e-05], [" ic", -10.765507698059082]]}, {"t": "px", "lp": -4.732720844913274e-05, "top": [["px", -4.732720844913274e-05], ["pz", -12.313774108886719]]}, {"t": " \\", "lp": -0.0015915177064016461, "top": [[" \\", -0.0015915177064016461], ["\n", -7.9806084632873535]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.0006265814881771803, "top": [["\n", -0.0006265814881771803], [".", -11.109360694885254]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function \u2014 Step by Step\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line. Note that the function appears to be **cut off** at the end (the last `-DGGML_SYCL_DEVICE` flag is incomplete), so I'll explain what's shown and flag the truncation.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (paths to `icx`/`icpx` compilers, libraries, etc.). The `--force` flag forces re-sourcing even if already sourced. Without this, the SYCL compilers wouldn't be on your `PATH`.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nStands for \"exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status.\" This is standard in build functions so a failed compile stops the build rather than continuing.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n- `-S`: source directory (the cloned repo)\n- `-B`: build directory\n- `-G Ninja`: use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, mentioned in `makedepends`)\n\n### Build type and install paths\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n```\nOptimized build (`-O3`, no debug symbols). This aligns with the `options=(!debug)` flag noted above.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n```\nInstalls binaries to `/usr` and libraries to `/usr/lib`.\n\n### The SYCL compilers\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx \\\n"}